{
  "timeline": [
    {
      "speaker": "Peter",
      "text": "What's the OWASP Top 10?",
      "start_s": 0.0,
      "end_s": 1.776
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Stewie",
      "text": "The ten most critical web app risks. Broken access control and injection lead the list.",
      "start_s": 1.926,
      "end_s": 6.606
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Peter",
      "text": "How do I stop injection?",
      "start_s": 6.756,
      "end_s": 8.388
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Stewie",
      "text": "Parameterized queries. Separate code from data so input can't become commands.",
      "start_s": 8.538,
      "end_s": 13.026
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Peter",
      "text": "And XSS?",
      "start_s": 13.176,
      "end_s": 14.952
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Stewie",
      "text": "Output encoding in the right context. HTML, URL, JavaScript \u2014 each needs its own escape.",
      "start_s": 15.102,
      "end_s": 20.838
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Peter",
      "text": "What about user input?",
      "start_s": 20.988,
      "end_s": 22.596
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Stewie",
      "text": "Validate everything server-side. Type, length, range, format. Treat input as hostile.",
      "start_s": 22.746,
      "end_s": 28.53
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Peter",
      "text": "Access control?",
      "start_s": 28.68,
      "end_s": 30.456
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Stewie",
      "text": "Enforce authorization on every request, server-side, and fail closed. Never trust the client.",
      "start_s": 30.606,
      "end_s": 36.078
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Peter",
      "text": "Secrets in code?",
      "start_s": 36.228,
      "end_s": 38.004
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Stewie",
      "text": "Never. Use secret stores and workload identity instead of hardcoded credentials.",
      "start_s": 38.154,
      "end_s": 42.522
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Peter",
      "text": "Don't firewalls fix this?",
      "start_s": 42.672,
      "end_s": 44.448
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Stewie",
      "text": "WAFs and CSP supplement secure code. They never replace it.",
      "start_s": 44.598,
      "end_s": 48.702
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Peter",
      "text": "How do I catch flaws early?",
      "start_s": 48.852,
      "end_s": 50.556
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Stewie",
      "text": "SAST for static analysis, SCA for dependencies, both in CI.",
      "start_s": 50.706,
      "end_s": 54.738
    }
  ],
